  "verifiedFindings": [
    "Article B-4.2 and the dated bachelor programme list 31 positive-credit components and a total of 180 EC. The third-year integration subject is listed as Tax Law from an Economic Perspective in the dated catalogue. The four Amsterdam Law Firm courses are zero-credit components across years one and two.",
    "Article B-4.5 and the course entry require 120 EC for the 6 EC thesis, with results posted before the registration deadline, a fiscal legal topic and oral defence. Article B-7.1 lists a 42 EC first-year study advice threshold, subject to the regulation.",
    "The 3 EC European Tax Law course is compulsory in both the OER and programme catalogue. Its admission condition remains unresolved. The credit allocation and substantive academic identity are supported independently of that enrolment condition."
  ],
  "essentialEvidence": "Confirm how regular 2026-entry Tax Law bachelor students satisfy the published minor-enrolment condition for compulsory Foundations of European Tax Law (3313GEBRVY).",
  "officialAlternative": "Located the adopted 2026–2027 faculty regulations via the Tax Law bachelor selection and the separate dated programme catalogue. OER B-4.2 and the bachelor catalogue both require the 3 EC course in year three. OER B-5.2 delegates additional course entry requirements to the catalogue. The linked course entry for 3313GEBRVY lists enrolment in the business taxation minor and gives no rule for regular Tax Law bachelor students. The official minor page confirms it shares these courses with the degree but describes minor admission separately. The faculty change overview and supplementary regulations did not identify a bachelor-specific rule or correction.",
  "nextAction": "Resume CP396 with official source attempt two. Check the bachelor-specific UvA course registration guidance, formal errata or a dated official course variant for 3313GEBRVY. Resolve whether regular Tax Law bachelor enrolment satisfies or replaces the listed minor condition. Retain the 31 verified component identities and credit values, 69 interest rows and feasible provisional UCR trials. Then reassess the provisional tax-law comparability judgment and finish stages 1 and 3–6."
}
